Gas and vacuum sources — books, methods and primary evidence (@gas-sources: 0, is #chapter) { r_0KQ1MK1BQV5KMNS3DVQT2N1VXB
Begin with the complete vacuum handbook, then read the full cryogenic and adsorption courses progressively. Baglin and Kersevan provide a complete 80-page vacuum course with exercises and solutions; Chiggiato and Taborelli deepen pump, thermal and manufactured-surface mechanisms. The source Records specify editions, inspected material, access and reuse conditions. Primary research and metrology reports deepen the methods and their limits.

- [Fundamentals of Vacuum Technology — Walter Umrath and contributors](sources/Fundamentals-of-Vacuum-Technology-Leybold.lingua#r_1S93A5X32978GSHZH4CF96VPQR)
